        <headline>Wind Advisory issued September 26 at 1:17PM EDT until September 27 at 12:00PM EDT by NWS Mount Holly NJ</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...North winds 10 to 20 mph with gusts up to 50 mph.

* WHERE...In New Jersey, Sussex and Warren Counties. In Pennsylvania,
Berks, Lehigh, Northampton, Carbon, and Monroe Counties.

* WHEN...Until noon EDT Sunday.

* IMPACTS...Gusty winds will blow around unsecured objects. Tree
limbs could be blown down and a few power outages may result.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...While there may be a lull in winds later today
into this evening, winds are expected to increase again overnight
into Sunday morning.
</description>
        <instruction>Winds this strong can make driving difficult, especially for high
profile vehicles. Use extra caution.</instruction>
